<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Slivnitsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbo-bulgarian-war">Serbo-Bulgarian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Slivnitsa was fought from 17 to 19 November 1885 near the town of Slivnitsa, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofia">Sofia</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbo-bulgarian-war">Serbo-Bulgarian War</a>. The Bulgarian army under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-of-battenberg">Alexander of Battenberg</a> defeated the invading Serbian army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> I. The victory secured the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> with Eastern Rumelia, proclaimed in September 1885, which the powers accepted in 1886.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-slivnitsa.jpg" alt="Battle of Slivnitsa" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitar Gjudzenov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Slivnitsa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
